        {
          "path": "_m/g/c/4/n/cobh-wp/cobh-pronounced-cove-cobh-dry-.jpg",
          "filename": "Cobh (pronounced Cove) \"Cobh Dry Cleaners\" (7174125569).jpg",
          "caption": "The Napoleonic Wars meant the town became a British Naval port with its own admiral and much of the present day buildings were built. The cessation of hostilities dented its prosperity for a time but it became widely known as a health resort and many convalescents came to Cove to avail of its temperate climate. Amongst these was Rev. Charles Wolfe who wrote \"The Burial of Sir John Moore After Corunna\" and whose remains are buried in the Old Church Cemetery outside the town.",
          "alt": "The Napoleonic Wars meant the town became a British Naval port with its own admiral and much of the present day buildings were built. The cessation of hostilities dented its prosperity for a time but it became widely known as a health resort and many convalescents came to Cove to avail of its temperate climate. Amongst these was Rev. Charles Wolfe who wrote \"The Burial of Sir John Moore After Corunna\" and whose remains are buried in the Old Church Cemetery outside the town.",
